1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Roll two dice. Which total should you bet on?

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:08,000
The totals run two to twelve. Eleven of them.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,200
But dice do not roll totals. They roll pairs.

4
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:16,000
There are thirty-six pairs, and six of them make seven.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:20,800
One and six. Two and five. Three and four, and back again.

6
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:25,200
Twelve needs double six. One pair out of thirty-six.

7
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:31,200
So seven turns up six times as often as twelve.

8
00:00:31,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Eleven totals, thirty-six rolls. That is the whole trick.
